Subject: [PATCH 07869/11362] [outer-loop] cd82 residual DIAGNOSED: budget-wall
 variance of the uniform draw, shared by the reference -- deliberately NOT
 patched

The 1-of-9 residual is not a capability loss and not caused by the click gate.

ATTRIBUTION: B2 (gate ON) and B2_nofix (gate OFF) lose cd82 recoloured IDENTICALLY on seed
20260724 -> the gate is causally irrelevant. Every GREEDY-draw arm solves it (A, B, C, D all
levels=1); only the uniform-draw arms miss it, on one seed. Arm E -- just-explore ITSELF -- also
loses cd82 recoloured on one of its seeds, so this is a property of uniform-random draw rather
than a Carnot defect.

BUDGET PROBE: 2000 -> levels=0 using 1977 of 2000 actions (AT THE WALL, not stuck);
3000 -> 0 (2967 actions); 4000 -> levels=1 (3930 actions). Budget-recoverable.

NO CODE CHANGE, deliberately. The only way to remove this variance is to make the within-tier
draw less uniform -- but the uniform draw is exactly what carries the gains (B2 beats greedy B by
2-3 games and stays colour-robust where B degrades 9->8 under recolour). Patching it to rescue one
near-budget cell would remove the working mechanism. The budget was also NOT raised for the
definitive run: that would make the numbers non-comparable with every prior run in this series.
The failing cell stays in the denominator rather than being excused.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01JntPrUGLNesPcJH1pyfFYw
